# tests/arc-manifest.ttl — the arc's denominator (spec 2026-08-20 §3), hand-authored.
#
# SEED STATE: the five settled rungs and ZERO criteria. Every rung therefore renders
# `?` on the cockpit strip — unknown is NOT zero (spec §4, decision 6), and a rung with
# no criteria is deliberately not a refusal. The ~42 criteria are authored by later
# tasks of this loop.
#
# `prog:` (https://w3id.org/iladub/progress#) is repo-internal and unpublished, exactly
# as `cor:` and `dg:` are: it is not w3id-registered and never appears in vocab/ontology/.
#
# Two rules this file lives under:
#   - CODE NEVER WRITES THIS FILE (spec §9; the cor: precedent). It is validated, by
#     tests/arc-shapes.ttl + tests/test_arc_manifest.py, and hand-edited in reviewed
#     commits — never auto-flipped to met.
#   - RUNGS ARE UNORDERED (decision 8). There is no prog:precedes and no index property:
#     `tab` is depth inside `etkl`, not a stage after `substrate`, so the repo does not
#     assert an ordering that is false for one of the five.
#
# Criterion IRIs are `prog:criterion:<rungKey>:<slug>` and must agree with prog:ofRung
# (M9/M9b). That is not tidiness: scripts/cockpit.py must read this file WITHOUT rdflib
# (its performance contract, cockpit.py:34-38), and a regex read is safe only over a
# file where every criterion is a top-level IRI subject encoding its own rung.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix prog: <https://w3id.org/iladub/progress#> .

# The runner these assertions were validated against — M5's third arm (spec §7.2.2).
# "If CI is green, every oracle is green" is true only RELATIVE TO A RUNNER: under the
# system python3 the corpus battery reports false reds and pyrudof is simply absent.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-20 on this tree:
#   $ ./.venv/bin/python -c "import sys,rdflib;print(sys.executable, sys.version.split()[0], rdflib.__version__)"
#   /Volumes/WD Green/dev/git/iladub/.venv/bin/python 3.12.0 7.6.0
#
# Recorded to the precision that is an assertion rather than an accident:
#   - prog:interpreter is the repo-relative runner named by tests/test_corpus.py:7, not
#     the absolute path, which is this machine's and not this repo's.
#   - prog:pythonVersion is the FEATURE version. .github/workflows/ci.yml pins
#     python-version "3.12" and floats the patch, so "3.12.0" would be a fact about this
#     laptop. The check is dotted-prefix equality, so the recorded precision IS the
#     assertion: record more digits and more is refused.
#   - prog:rdflibVersion is recorded in full, so the check on it is exact. 7.1.4 (the
#     system python3) is what §7.2.2 measured as producing false reds.
prog:manifest a prog:Manifest ;
    rdfs:label "the arc's denominator" ;
    prog:interpreter ".venv/bin/python" ;
    prog:pythonVersion "3.12" ;
    prog:rdflibVersion "7.6.0" .

# The five settled rungs (decision 8), named and never numbered. Labels are the section
# headings of docs/narrative/scope-evolution.md.

prog:rung:etkl a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "etkl" ;
    rdfs:label "the document compiler" .

prog:rung:tab a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "tab" ;
    rdfs:label "reading depth, inside the compiler" .

prog:rung:dec a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "dec" ;
    rdfs:label "decidability, the context graph" .

prog:rung:holon a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "holon" ;
    rdfs:label "the reframe, from record to active holon" .

prog:rung:substrate a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "substrate" ;
    rdfs:label "the membrane enforced at runtime" .
